From: cnjn
Subject: [PATCH] fw4: probe hardware flow offload per lower device

A bridge can contain software-only ports, and an automatically created
IPv6 interface can report a PPP device as its carrier. Neither can bind a
hardware flowtable, but they must not disable offload on the supported
lower devices. Resolve stacked devices first, then probe each candidate.
Keep the combined probe so incompatible device combinations still fall
back to software, as does a candidate set with no supported devices.

--- a/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
+++ b/root/usr/share/ucode/fw4.uc
@@ -566,9 +566,13 @@
 		if (!devices)
 			return null;
 
-		devices = sort(uniq(devices));
-
-		if (!nft_try_hw_offload(devices)) {
+		/* Software-only bridge ports and PPP carriers must not disable
+		 * hardware offload on the other resolved lower devices.
+		 */
+		devices = filter(sort(uniq(devices)),
+			device => nft_try_hw_offload([device]));
+
+		if (!length(devices) || !nft_try_hw_offload(devices)) {
 			this.warn('Hardware flow offloading unavailable, falling back to software offloading');
 			this.state.defaults.flow_offloading_hw = false;
 
